  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Strengthening health services and cross-border cooperation at the Haitian-Dominican border</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This action aims to improve stability in the Haiti&#xbf;Dominican Republic border area by expanding access to essential maternal, newborn, sexual and reproductive, and child health services in selected Haitian border zones, especially for women, children and other vulnerable people on the move. It will also strengthen practical, gender-responsive and rights-based cross-border cooperation to better protect migrants, returnees, displaced people and host communities.The action has two main objectives: first, to improve the availability, accessibility and quality of health and SRHR services in Haitian border areas through support to facilities, equipment, referrals and frontline providers; second, to improve technical cooperation between Haitian and Dominican stakeholders for safer, more coordinated responses to cross-border mobility. Overall, it is expected to improve access to care, continuity of services, and protection-sensitive case management in a highly fragile context.</narrative>
  </description>
